<title>UK: IMG declines comment on Man Utd report.</title>
<headline>IMG declines comment on Man Utd report.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-10-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>Sports marketing agency IMG declined comment on Monday on a report that it was pondering a bid for English soccer champions Manchester United.</p>
<p>&quot;We never make comments on unsubstantiated press stories,&quot; said an official at the London office of the U.S. agency.</p>
<p>The official said it was &quot;common knowledge&quot; that IMG was interested in increasing its involvement in soccer in general.</p>
<p>Britain's Sunday Express newspaper reported at the weekend that IMG was a likely bidder for United.</p>
<p>The latest bid rumours helped to fuel further steep gains in Man Utd stock which added 56 1/2p to 570p. United shares had put on 61p on Friday as bid talk first surfaced.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 7717</p>
</text>
